title: A Million Marks
subtitle: Wages are paid twice a day and spent within the hour.
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: year = 1923 and month = 7
max-visits: 1
on-arrival: {!
RG.news('The dollar passes a million marks', 3);
Q.inflation = Math.min(100, Q.inflation + 8);
Q.stability -= 5;
!}

= A Million Marks

At the end of July the dollar passes a million marks. In some works wages are paid twice a day, and wives wait at the gates with shopping bags to spend them before the next price list goes up. The unions are bankrupt, because the dues are worthless before they reach the treasurer. Hundreds of thousands are leaving them, and the party's offices cannot print membership cards fast enough.

- @doors: Open the doors to everyone.
- @gold: Demand wages in gold value through the factory councils.

@doors
subtitle: Many new members, untrained and angry. The party will be harder to steer.
on-arrival: {!
for (var d of Q.districts) {
    Q['district_' + d + '_members'] *= 1.12;
}
Q.e23_inflation_line = 3;
Q.unity -= 8;
!}

The new members have never been to a meeting. They are waiting for someone to tell them what to do.

@gold
subtitle: [? if lock_councils = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] A demand every worker understands. The Berlin councils start to meet every week.
choose-if: lock_councils < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids it.
on-arrival: {!
if (!RG.e22) { this._runActions(this.game.scenes.e22_lib.onArrival); }
RG.e22.against('councils');
Q.e23_inflation_line = 2;
RG.district('berlin', {loyalty: 5, militancy: 5});
Q.worker_support += 5;
!}

Council after council votes for wages fixed in gold marks and paid in paper at the day's rate. In Berlin the councils of the big works start to meet every week in a union hall on the Engelufer.
